# Daily backup — crontab alternative to the systemd timer (backup.timer).
# Install:  crontab -e   then paste (edit the absolute path).
#
# Cron has no per-line timezone, so this assumes the HOST clock is Asia/Taipei.
# If your host runs UTC, use 07:30 (= 15:30 Asia/Taipei) instead — Taiwan has no DST,
# so the offset is a constant +8h.
#
# BACKUP_DEST (the backup mount, e.g. /mnt/nas/qt-backup) MUST be provided. The line
# below sources .env first (`set -a && . ./.env`), so define BACKUP_DEST there. The
# script exits 1 with a clear message + Discord alert if BACKUP_DEST is unset/unmounted.
#
# Fields: min hour dom mon dow  command
# 30 15 * * *  → 15:30 every day. Weekend/holiday runs are cheap no-ops for pg (the
# telemetry just hasn't changed) and harmless mirrors for reports/ + data/parquet*.

30 15 * * *  cd "$HOME/Quantitative_Trading/backtest_platform" && set -a && . ./.env && set +a && /usr/bin/env bash deploy/backup.sh >> "$HOME/Quantitative_Trading/backtest_platform/reports/backup.cron.log" 2>&1
